  "worked_solution": "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{2}{5}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{2}{5}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
